WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.000
On a cache hit, the entry’s pointer selects the bytes returned by a file read.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:10.000
Placement is checked first: the overflow must reach an owned cache entry.

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:14.000
The path-normalization copy exceeds its 0x301-byte temporary buffer.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:18.000
Forged range, dirty state and pointer make the cache hit reach fs memory.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:23.000
The same read now returns bytes from fs memory.

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:29.000
CONTROL maps cache metadata. DATA maps the selected memory.

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:35.000
CONTROL changes the pointer. DATA reads or writes through it.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:38.000
The marker matched. Now restore the original bytes.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:40.000
Change the pointer. Change where the bytes go.
